  "name": "OpenTSLM",
  "alternateName": [
    "Open Time Series Language Models",
    "TSLMs"
  ],
  "description": "Family of Time Series Language Models (TSLMs) from Stanford Biodesign for Digital Health (BDHG) that integrate time series as a native modality into pretrained LLMs, enabling natural-language prompting and reasoning over multivariate clinical time series of any length. Supports 12-lead ECG question answering, EEG sleep stage classification, and human activity recognition from accelerometry. Two architecture variants: Soft Prompt (SP) and Flamingo. Available as Llama 3.2 (1B/3B) and Gemma 3 fine-tuned variants on HuggingFace. Accepted at ICML 2026 (Deep Learning / LLM main track). 1,200+ GitHub stars. Real-world adoption: Seattle Children's Hospital adopted OpenTSLM for pediatric ECG analysis toward a cardiac ICU clinical decision-support foundation model. Consortium includes researchers from major frontier AI labs and universities. MIT, Python.",
  "url": "https://github.com/StanfordBDHG/OpenTSLM",
